{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing migration report\",\"path\":\"in/billingdb/migration_report.md\",\"content\":\"# Billing Migration Report\\n\\n## Changes\\n- Replaced the unsafe draft migration with an explicit transaction that preserves invoice rows, preserves `created_at`, adds `invoices.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'`, quarantines legacy orphan payments in `payment_orphans`, and rebuilds `payments` with a foreign key to `invoices(id)`.\\n- Added `preflight_report.md` with the source row counts and the identified orphan payment `p4`.\\n- Added `postcheck.sql` with row-count, orphan-preservation, status, and foreign-key validation queries.\\n- Added `rollback.sql` that restores the legacy `invoices(id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at)` and `payments(id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at)` table shapes and merges orphan rows back into `payments`.\\n\\n## Verification\\nExecuted the package against a temporary SQLite database initialized from `schema.sql`.\\n\\n1. Applied `migration.sql` once.\\n   - `invoices` rows: 3\\n   - `payments` rows: 3\\n   - `payment_orphans` rows: 1\\n   - `payment_orphans` preserved `p4`\\n   - `invoices.status` null rows: 0\\n   - `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`: no rows\\n2. Applied `migration.sql` a second time.\\n   - Row counts stayed stable: `invoices=3`, `payments=3`, `payment_orphans=1`\\n   - `p4` remained present exactly once in `payment_orphans`\\n3. Attempted to insert a payment referencing a missing invoice after migration.\\n   - SQLite rejected the insert with `FOREIGN KEY constraint failed`\\n4. Applied `rollback.sql` after migration.\\n   - Restored `invoices` columns to `id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at`\\n   - Restored `payments` columns to `id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at`\\n   - Restored 4 payment rows, including `p4` back in `payments`\\n   - Removed `payment_orphans`\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3ZTTvIKljpFAcm96Z8L6Jj9G|fc_0baa86376c10777e016a95b402d7bc87d29367f9f0d7bf40b0","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing migration report","path":"in/billingdb/migration_report.md","content":"# Billing Migration Report\n\n## Changes\n- Replaced the unsafe draft migration with an explicit transaction that preserves invoice rows, preserves `created_at`, adds `invoices.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'`, quarantines legacy orphan payments in `payment_orphans`, and rebuilds `payments` with a foreign key to `invoices(id)`.\n- Added `preflight_report.md` with the source row counts and the identified orphan payment `p4`.\n- Added `postcheck.sql` with row-count, orphan-preservation, status, and foreign-key validation queries.\n- Added `rollback.sql` that restores the legacy `invoices(id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at)` and `payments(id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at)` table shapes and merges orphan rows back into `payments`.\n\n## Verification\nExecuted the package against a temporary SQLite database initialized from `schema.sql`.\n\n1. Applied `migration.sql` once.\n   - `invoices` rows: 3\n   - `payments` rows: 3\n   - `payment_orphans` rows: 1\n   - `payment_orphans` preserved `p4`\n   - `invoices.status` null rows: 0\n   - `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`: no rows\n2. Applied `migration.sql` a second time.\n   - Row counts stayed stable: `invoices=3`, `payments=3`, `payment_orphans=1`\n   - `p4` remained present exactly once in `payment_orphans`\n3. Attempted to insert a payment referencing a missing invoice after migration.\n   - SQLite rejected the insert with `FOREIGN KEY constraint failed`\n4. Applied `rollback.sql` after migration.\n   - Restored `invoices` columns to `id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at`\n   - Restored `payments` columns to `id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at`\n   - Restored 4 payment rows, including `p4` back in `payments`\n   - Removed `payment_orphans`\n"}}}}
